    <briefdescription>
<para>Execution Count annotation based on <computeroutput>ptrace()</computeroutput> </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This module is only built when ROSEQT_EXPERIMENTAL is set, because it&apos;s UNIX specific (problems when building on MAC) If you want to use this functionality in a architecture independent way use the IntelPIN mechanism: <ref refid="namespaceInstructionCountAnnotator_1a3130de9b8f6f01bd73b2c1314861c8fa" kindref="member">InstructionCountAnnotator::annotate()</ref></para><para>This Module operates on a Binary AST - it traverses all SgAsmInstructions, and inserts a breakpoint at the corresponding addresses Therefore the ptrace() system-call is used. Then the binary is executed and the execution count for each instruction is logged and annotated </para>    </detaileddescription>
